From 392855726a84213fddaec328407d5b8f75ea303b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler South <tsouth2@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:26:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 133/133] Name a Linux host in guest notices

Compatibility revision 55 delivers Linux host wording, flag-selected desktop labels, and the Linux-only digest-gated clock repair from Linux patches 0116 and 0117. Windows desktop labels and time-zone protocol stay unchanged. Record legacy lineage atomically before extraction, validate it on retries, and use the stricter SSH cutoff for ambiguous revisions. Select host power wording after catch-up without changing the Windows payloads.
